## 8. Zabbix Data Model

Use Zabbix 7.x JSON-RPC API, primarily `history.push`.

### Central job reporting

Create a dedicated logical Zabbix host:

`AAP-MONITORING`

Create one stable Text trapper master item per approved logical Desired State job.

Example keys:

```text
aap.ds.raw[PROD,DOMAIN_A]
aap.ds.raw[DEV,DOMAIN_A]
aap.ds.raw[TEST,DOMAIN_B]
```

Each daily execution creates a new timestamped history value for the same master item.

The AAP execution job ID is stored inside the JSON; it is not the Zabbix item ID.

### Host-level reporting

Use the existing Zabbix Windows hosts.

Create host-level Text trapper items such as:

```text
aap.host.desired_state.raw
aap.host.patching.raw
aap.host.provisioning.raw
```

The callback maps Ansible inventory hostnames to Zabbix technical hostnames.

Hostname mapping must be configurable and validated.

### Dependent items

Use JSONPath preprocessing to extract numerical values from the raw JSON.

Examples:

```text
$.job.duration_seconds
$.hosts.failed
$.hosts.unreachable
$.hosts.passed
$.tasks.changed
$.rates.host_success_pct
```

Create dependent items as numeric values for Zabbix history, trends, graphs, triggers, and dashboards.

Retain raw JSON for detailed historical analysis.

Use appropriate retention settings, initially targeting 90 days of detailed history subject to Zabbix capacity testing.

