## 14. Design Principles and Scope Control

Preserve the following architectural decisions:

- One reusable aggregate callback.
- YAML-driven job classification and KPI schema.
- Default-deny reporting.
- Logical reporting names independent of AAP template names.
- Job-level and host-level reporting.
- Zabbix 7.x as the existing monitoring backend.
- Final-only API publication.
- Three total delivery attempts.
- Bounded batches, memory, and publication time.
- No new infrastructure.
- No reporting roles added to existing playbooks.
- No impact on automation success/failure.
- Minimal Python complexity.
- Standard Ansible collection packaging.
- Reusable across multiple repositories.

**Do not overengineer the solution.**

Approach the implementation as a senior Ansible/AAP platform engineer designing a reusable enterprise component. Challenge incorrect assumptions, verify the Ansible callback API and Zabbix API against official documentation, and prioritize correctness, performance, maintainability, and operational simplicity over feature count.

The immediate next step is to review this specification, finalize the metric semantics and configuration contract, and implement the complete collection incrementally with tests and actual AAP/Zabbix integration validation.
